# Local run artifacts. Neither is produced by anything committed: `arol.json`
# is the config the README tells the reader to write for their own box ("the
# repo ships no arol.json"), so it carries an absolute store path that is true
# on exactly one machine, and `live-ask-out/` is the --out directory the live
# `ask` runs were pointed at by hand. The committed evidence for that path is
# docs/reports/ask-live-sample/, which is deliberate and stays tracked.
/arol.json
/live-ask-out/

/build-verify/
/build-gpu-tests/

# Secrets. The project reads ANTHROPIC_API_KEY from the environment and has
# never used a .env file -- these entries exist so that creating one cannot
# commit a key by accident.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
